# Root .env.example — for the optional Docker Compose web deployment
# (docker-compose.yaml: caddy + web). Not needed for local dev (`cd frontend && pnpm dev`)
# or the Android build — those use frontend/.env instead (see frontend/.env.example).
#
# NOTE: nothing in docker-compose.yaml currently reads a root .env file — the `web` service's
# env_file points at frontend/.env, and the `caddy` service has no env_file/environment at all,
# so SITE_ADDRESS below has no effect until that's wired up. This file is a placeholder for
# that future wiring, not a confirmed-working config today.

# Consumed by the Caddyfile ({$SITE_ADDRESS::80}) if/when the caddy service is given this
# variable. Your domain, e.g. "traxy.example.com". Leave unset to bind to :80 on all interfaces.
SITE_ADDRESS=
